cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Pseudolife-MCP in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Pseudolife-MCP: persistent long-term memory for MCP coding agents"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Pseudogiant-xr"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pseudogiant-xr/Pseudolife-MCP"
url: "https://github.com/Pseudogiant-xr/Pseudolife-MCP"
abstract: >-
  An MCP server giving coding agents durable long-term memory: an
  associative store with aging and supersession, a slot-keyed
  canonical-fact cortex with full version history, consolidation of the
  memory stream into facts and a knowledge graph, procedural lessons
  from outcome signals, and cited world facts. Benchmarked on
  LongMemEval with committed evidence artifacts.
keywords:
  - memory
  - model-context-protocol
  - llm-agents
  - knowledge-graph
  - retrieval
